Let $A_{i}O=a_{i},$ $A_{i}A_{j}=1$ and $\angle A_{1}A_{0}A_{3}=\angle A_{2}A_{0}A_{4}=90^{\circ},$
$\angle A_{1}A_{0}A_{2}=\angle A_{2}A_{0}A_{3}=\angle A_{3}A_{0}A_{4}=\angle A_{1}A_{0}A_{4}=120^{\circ}.$
By using the cosine law in $\triangle A_{i}OA_{j},$ we obtain the following system of equations with respect to $a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}:$

\begin{equation}\label{eqt12}
a_{1}^2+a_{2}^2=1,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}\label{eqt13}
a_{1}^2+a_{3}^2 +a_{1}a_{3}=1,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}\label{eqt14}
a_{1}^2+a_{4}^2 +a_{1}a_{4}=1,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}\label{eqt24}
a_{2}^2+a_{4}^2 +a_{2}a_{4}=1,
\end{equation}

The system of four equations (\ref{eqt12}), (\ref{eqt13}), (\ref{eqt14}), (\ref{eqt24}  does not have a positive real solution with respect to $(a_{1},a_{2},a_{3},a_{4}).$
